Test (ubuntu-24.04 / specification) shard 1/4	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-25T05:19:35.9612725Z   left: "## How to do spec driven development\n\n1. Spec-First — Specs seed the initial generation, then code is allowed to drift. Good for AI-assisted features and prototypes. Low overhead, no long-term guarantees.\n2. Spec-Anchored — Specs and code evolve together as living documentation; automated tests enforce alignment. Piskala's paper calls this \"the sweet spot for most production systems.\"\n3. Spec-as-Source — Humans edit only the spec; code is fully generated and never hand-edited.\n\n### Sources\n- web_page → https://dev.to/krlz/spec-driven-development-in-2026-what-it-is-the-tooling-and-how-teams-actually-use-it-2fk2 (Varies (per page): )"
